## added some extra features
To ensure your system works out-of-the-box across broad hardware—from consumer motherboards (ASUS, MSI, ASRock, Intel) to laptops (Dell Latitude 7370, 7480, Acer, ASUS Vivo)—the package can be expanded with pre-bundled firmware dependencies and an Automated Driver Caching & Hotplug USB Loader.
​🛠️ Key Additions Included in the Build
​Pre-Bundled Broad Vendor Drivers & Firmware:
​Intel Ethernet & Wi-Fi: firmware-iwlwifi covers Intel Wireless AC 7265, 8260, 8265 (Dell Latitude 7370 / 7480) and Intel Gigabit/10G Ethernet NICs (I217, I218, I219, e1000e).
​Realtek Ethernet & Wi-Fi: firmware-realtek covers RTL8111/8168/8411 PCIe Gigabit LAN found on ASUS, MSI, ASRock, Acer, and Vivo boards.
​Broadcom & Atheros: firmware-misc-nonfree / firmware-atheros covers extra legacy and mobile network hardware.
​Automated USB Hotplug Driver Scanner & Cache Daemon:
​A background worker (berry-driver-loader.service) monitors connected PCI/USB hardware via udevadm and lspci.
​When a USB flash drive containing driver packages (.deb) is inserted, the loader automatically detects missing driver modules, installs them onto the system, and saves them to a local cache at /var/cache/berry-router/drivers/.
